# What never enters git, grouped by what produces it.
#
# This file is a verdict, not a convenience: the pre-commit hook refuses any staged path
# it matches, and `redeploy-web` lays it into every collaborator's clone (scripts/setup/user.sh).
# A pattern with no slash matches at any depth.

# Dotfiles: machine-local state, never shared (.venv, .state, .cache, .idea, .mypy_cache,
# .claude, .mcp.json, solutions/.progress.html). The tracked ones are re-included at the end.
.*

# The root CLAUDE.md: a symlink onto the tracked packages/solver/solver/ai/claude/CLAUDE.md.
/CLAUDE.md

# Python: bytecode, and what `pip install -e` and wheel builds leave beside the sources.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Compiled solutions: scripts/c/compile.sh writes pNNNN_sK_c beside its source, and any
# shared object is a binary all the same. The git hooks and `make audit` refuse binaries too.
*_c
*.so

# The content wheel's generated parts. scripts/content/stage.py makes them in its scratch copy,
# never here; ignored so a staging run pointed at the checkout cannot commit a second public tree.
packages/content/euler_content/tree/
packages/content/euler_content/_version.py

# Security-review working material: findings, host captures, probes, test credentials. Local and
# confidential by design — the repo is public, and docs/ is published on the site.
/audit/

# Re-include the tracked dotfiles. These must stay last: the last matching pattern wins.
!.gitattributes
!.gitignore
!.shellcheckrc
